# Platform Deliverables

## Purpose

Make every commercial project deliver native to each platform it targets:
declared deliverables, designed reframes, planned durations, and edits that
survive a mute autoplaying feed.

## Scope

Applies only when `production_type` in `production/project.yaml` is
`commercial` (spot, social, branded-content, music-video). Layers on top of
`rules/common/` and the domain layers without contradicting them.

## Core Principles

- A deliverable is a designed artifact, not an export setting. Each
  platform/ratio/duration combination is planned from blocking onward.
- Native beats adapted: a 9:16 vertical conceived as vertical always beats a
  16:9 frame cropped after the fact.
- The feed is hostile: assume sound off, thumb hovering, UI covering the
  frame edges.

## Declaring Deliverables

- Every commercial project MUST declare `deliverables[]` in
  `production/project.yaml`; each entry carries `platform`, `aspect_ratio`,
  and `duration_seconds_max`. An empty or missing `deliverables[]` fails
  validation.
- The first entry is primary and drives default framing; every other entry
  MUST still be planned per the rules below, never exported as an
  afterthought.

## Native-Format Discipline

- A 9:16 vertical is a reframe DESIGNED at blocking and storyboard time —
  subject placement, headroom, and action staged so the extraction composes
  alone. NEVER deliver a lazy center-crop of a horizontal master.
- Framing MUST respect platform UI safe areas: captions, progress bars,
  buttons, and username overlays occupy frame edges; nothing essential
  (faces, product, supers) sits under them.
- Captions and supers are planned per deliverable — burned in or placed for
  the platform's caption layer — and reviewed at storyboard, not bolted on
  in the edit.

## Duration Economy

- 15/30/60-second versions are separate edits with their own edit plans and
  structure — a 15 is not a trimmed 30. Each cut MUST stand alone: complete
  message, complete brand resolution.
- Every deliverable's runtime MUST fit its `duration_seconds_max`; shot
  lists are planned against the shortest cut first so nothing essential
  exists only in the long version.

## Hook and Sound-Off Structure

- The first 2 seconds of every cut MUST hold a scroll: motion, face,
  question, or visual surprise on screen immediately. NEVER open cold on a
  slow establishing build.
- Every cut MUST read fully with sound off — story, message, and brand
  legible mute via action, captions, and supers.

## Reframing in Shot Files

- One shot can carry multiple framings. Each shot file MUST record its
  per-deliverable reframes (which deliverables it serves, framing intent per
  ratio) so continuity and storyboard review see every extraction.
- Prompt packages MUST be compiled per deliverable aspect ratio — one
  variant per ratio in `production/prompts/`, each within the provider's
  supported `aspectRatios`. NEVER generate one ratio and crop to the others.

## Validation

- `scripts/validate.js` requires a non-empty `deliverables[]` (each entry
  with `platform`, `aspect_ratio`, `duration_seconds_max`) on commercial
  projects and checks prompt-package ratios against provider capabilities.
- Shot files whose reframe list omits a declared deliverable are flagged at
  shot-list review.
- Hook strength, safe-area compliance, and mute readability are human
  review at storyboard and edit-plan approval.
